  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Re-routing keeps persistence, and the plain reading needs long rings",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For networks of rule-60 rings with equally spaced law-(12,12) contacts: (1) re-routing at any set of contacts (exchanging which ring each arriving ring continues on there, Chmutov's partial duality) keeps every arc of the contact graph, so every contact's persistence, and the maps sharing a contact graph are exactly its 2^E re-routings; (2) the line network of the n x n square torus (re-routed at every vertical contact), n >= 3, has 2n rings of 2n contacts whose ring graph is a cycle, keeps every contact persistent and is on time, every ring having a closest contact reached by exactly one shortest route; computed likewise for the triangular and honeycomb line networks, n = 3 to 20; (3) with the contact graph of a square torus whose lattice has no nonzero vector shorter than 2^(k+3) in taxicab length, a ring whose contacts fit in a box of side 2^k - 2 is late, so an on-time network with the contact graph of the n x n square torus, n >= 64, has at most 64n rings, each of at least n/8 - 4 contacts.",
